  "disposition": "COMPLETE_TAGGED_TYPE_AND_PRIME_LABEL_PREDICATE_SEAMS_MATERIALIZED_UNCOMPILED",
  "review_notes": [
    "Every1064B original and2650B organized byte read individually. Place is precisely an inductive with distinguished archimedean constructor and finite:Nat->Place, plus complete DecidableEq/Repr deriving. The finite constructor accepts every Nat, not just primes; this is a tagged set of labels, not a valuation/absolute-value/completion theorem.",
    "The first complete seam keeps the inductive with deriving, exact IsArchimedeanPlace equality predicate and full constructor-disequality proof for arbitrary p:Nat. The proof is the original intro h;cases h, without extra assumptions.",
    "The second seam keeps the whole IsFinitePrimePlace existential/equality/Nat.Prime predicate, exact IsBadTMFPrime finite2-or-finite3 disjunction and complete bad_tmf_prime_is_finite proof under its original implicit v and h. Its conclusion is only an existential natural finite tag; it does not prove Nat.Prime of that witness or characterize all finite tags.",
    "The two complete groups use only an explicit import/open of the newly copied same-source tagged-type module. Original Folder.Basic import and full original module documentation remain exact in both outputs. No open Folder is added: its sole Basic provider has no actual Folder namespace declaration. No old imported Place provider or other source version is substituted. Namespace/component lookup remains unreplayed."
  ],
